Problem:
A farm co-op mixes 1,000 kg of cattle feed from corn, soybean meal and oats. Corn costs $0.30 per kg and is 10% protein and 3% fiber. Soybean meal costs $0.80 per kg and is 45% protein and 6% fiber. Oats cost $0.20 per kg and are 10% protein and 11% fiber. The feed must be at least 17% protein and at most 6% fiber by weight. How many kilograms of each ingredient should go into the feed to make it as cheaply as possible?

